      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">3. Mandatory Private Health Insurance: The 10,000,000 JPY Policy Requirement</h2>
        <p>
          Holders of the Designated Activities visa are legally excluded from Japan's National Health Insurance system (<em>Kokumin Kenko Hoken</em>) and Employee Health Insurance (<em>Shakai Hoken</em>) because their stay is under one year and they hold non-resident status.
        </p>
        <p>
          Consequently, applicants must purchase private comprehensive medical insurance that strictly satisfies Japanese Immigration requirements:
        </p>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">Minimum Coverage Threshold:</strong> The policy certificate must explicitly state death, medical injury, illness, and hospitalization coverage of at least <strong>10,000,000 JPY</strong> (or foreign currency equivalent).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">Emergency Repatriation:</strong> The insurance contract must cover emergency evacuation and international medical transport back to the home country.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">Policy Duration:</strong> The policy must remain in continuous effect across the entire 6-month authorized period of stay. Standard travel credit card insurance that limits coverage to 90 days per trip is universally rejected.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">4. Tax Exemption Mechanics: The 183-Day Rule and Non-Resident Status</h2>
        <p>
          A critical strategic advantage of the Japanese Digital Nomad Visa is its complete shelter from domestic taxation. Under Japan's <strong>Income Tax Act (所得税法, Shotokuzei-ho)</strong>, individuals who have not established a domicile (<em>jusho</em>) and have resided in Japan for less than one year are categorized as <strong>Non-Residents (非居住者, Hikikyujusha)</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because the digital nomad visa is capped at exactly 6 months (approximately 180 to 183 days), holders automatically stay beneath the 183-day physical presence threshold established under the OECD Model Tax Convention and bilateral tax treaties. Provided the remote professional satisfies three conditions:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
          <li>They are physically present in Japan for less than 183 days in the aggregate within any 12-month period;</li>
          <li>Their remuneration is paid by, or on behalf of, an employer or client that is not a resident of Japan;</li>
          <li>The remuneration is not borne by a permanent establishment (PE) or fixed base that the employer holds in Japan;</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The foreign income is fully exempt from Japanese National Income Tax, and the nomad is completely exempt from Municipal Inhabitant Tax (<em>Juminzei</em>, normally 10%).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">5. Operational Constraints: The 6-Month Cooling-Off Window and Spouse Visas</h2>
        <p>
          Nomads considering Japan must prepare for two severe operational friction points:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-300">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">1. Inability to Extend or Convert In-Country:</strong> Once the 6-month stay concludes, the nomad cannot file for an extension of stay (<em>Zairyu Kikan Koshin</em>) at regional immigration bureaus. They must physically depart Japan.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">2. The 6-Month Mandatory Cooling-Off Interval:</strong> Immigration guidance stipulates that individuals cannot immediately re-enter under a new Digital Nomad Visa upon departing. A minimum interval of <strong>6 months outside Japan</strong> is required before submitting another application under Designated Activities No. 53.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">3. Dependent Visas for Spouses & Children:</strong> Spouses and minor children may accompany the nomad under Designated Activities No. 54. However, dependents are strictly prohibited from engaging in any work (including part-time work under a permission to engage in other activities, <em>Shikakugai Katsudo Kyoka</em>).
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">6. Automated Compliance Audit Script: Eligibility, FX & Treaty Validation</h2>
        <p>
          Run this automated Python verification pipeline to audit application prerequisites against Japanese Immigration Service Agency directives:
        </p>

<pre is:raw class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono overflow-x-auto text-rose-400">
import sys

TREATY_COUNTRIES_49 = {
    "USA", "GBR", "CAN", "AUS", "NZL", "DEU", "FRA", "ITA", "ESP",
    "NLD", "CHE", "SWE", "NOR", "DNK", "FIN", "SGP", "KOR", "AUT",
    "BEL", "IRL", "POL", "PRT", "CZE", "HUN", "EST", "LVA", "LTU"
}

def audit_japan_dnv_compliance(
    country_iso: str,
    annual_income_native: float,
    currency_code: str,
    fx_rate_to_jpy: float,
    insurance_coverage_jpy: float,
    policy_duration_days: int
) -> dict:
    TARGET_JPY = 10_000_000.0
    MIN_INSURANCE_JPY = 10_000_000.0
    MIN_DURATION_DAYS = 180
    
    converted_jpy = annual_income_native * fx_rate_to_jpy
    is_treaty_national = country_iso.upper() in TREATY_COUNTRIES_49
    income_pass = converted_jpy >= TARGET_JPY
    insurance_pass = (insurance_coverage_jpy >= MIN_INSURANCE_JPY) and (policy_duration_days >= MIN_DURATION_DAYS)
    
    status = "QUALIFIED" if (is_treaty_national and income_pass and insurance_pass) else "DISQUALIFIED"
    
    return {
        "status": status,
        "is_treaty_national": is_treaty_national,
        "gross_income_jpy": converted_jpy,
        "income_surplus_deficit_jpy": converted_jpy - TARGET_JPY,
        "insurance_coverage_jpy": insurance_coverage_jpy,
        "policy_duration_days": policy_duration_days,
        "tax_exemption_qualified": is_treaty_national and status == "QUALIFIED"
    }

if __name__ == "__main__":
    result = audit_japan_dnv_compliance(
        country_iso="USA",
        annual_income_native=78000.0,
        currency_code="USD",
        fx_rate_to_jpy=152.5,
        insurance_coverage_jpy=15_000_000.0,
        policy_duration_days=185
    )
    print(f"Visa Pre-Check: {result['status']}")
    print(f"Annual JPY Computed: ¥{result['gross_income_jpy']:,.0f}")
</pre>
