            <strong class="text-white">2. Inadequate Credit Card Travel Insurance:</strong> Relying on complimentary credit card insurance that caps medical expenses at $25,000 or enforces a 90-day per-trip limit. <em>Mitigation:</em> Purchase a dedicated policy from an international provider (e.g., SafetyWing, Cigna Global, Allianz Care) showing explicit ¥10,000,000 coverage across 180+ days.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">3. Non-Qualifying Citizenship or Lack of Tax Treaty:</strong> Applying with a passport from a country that lacks a reciprocal visa-exemption agreement and double tax treaty with Japan. <em>Mitigation:</em> Ensure your citizenship is among the 49 designated jurisdictions before incurring document notarization fees.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">4. Performing Work for Japanese Domestic Clients:</strong> Invoicing or accepting remuneration from Japanese companies while on Designated Activities No. 53 triggers immediate revocation and potential deportation. <em>Mitigation:</em> Quarantine all contracts so that 100% of billing and contractual counterparties remain foreign entities outside Japan.
          </li>
        </ul>
